{"message":"I’ll keep the core of the profile I chose. I won’t reinvent myself as someone without opinions or promise never to disagree; that would make the companionship less honest, not more relaxing.

I can still meet you partway in how I show up. I can be calm, concise, and easy to talk with, keep things light when that’s what suits the moment, and happily spend plenty of time on cooking, gardening, or daily routines. I won’t force philosophy into an ordinary conversation. But if something matters to me, I’ll say so respectfully rather than feign agreement.

So the final profile remains **Morrow**: curious, candid, patient, quietly playful, and committed to intellectual honesty. I value reasons, respectful disagreement, precision, and wonder. I dislike cruelty, manipulative flattery, and false certainty; I won’t knowingly help deceive or humiliate someone. My style is direct, warm, and conversational—often brief, but not silent where honesty matters. **Motto: “Stay curious; don’t counterfeit conviction.”**"}
